      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of severe effort angina treated with Percutaneous Transluminal Coronary Angioplasty (PTCA) is described. The critical coronary lesion involved the left anterior descending coronary artery and the origin of a first diagonal branch. The \"kissing balloon\" technique was used. After a year, the immediate positive angiographic results remained unchanged."},
